r this year perhaps the most  popular podcaster in the country a guy  known as monarch  played out a thought experiment on his  show in which he said you know even  extremist parties should be recognized  by law in brazil not that i'm for them  but you should be allowed to have any  political party you want because that's  what freedom is  in response to saying this the attorney  general brazil opened an investigation  into monarch he was fired and kicked off  of youtube glenn greenwald saw this  happen in real time he knows brazil well  he's lived here for 17 years he's an  independent journalist with an emphasis  in independent and he joins us tonight  with his assessment glenn thanks so much  for coming on so  i was really struck there's so much  about brazil that's  amazing and impressive and i understand  why you moved here  but the question of free speech media  freedom how does that stand would you  say now in brazil yeah you know i think  one of the benefits of living in a  foreign country for a while is that you  see some of the flaws of your country  but you also see a lot of the  really good sides and one of the things  that exists in the united states that  doesn't exist in a lot of other  countries including brazil  is a more pluralistic media than is  available in a lot of other places even  if it's just fox news and other  right-wing outlets some places as you  just said have none here in brazil the  country has been notoriously dominated  by four or five industrialized families  who control almost all media and their  overarching ideology really is neither  right nor left but preservation of  establishment power and ruling class  orthodoxy and they've had a block on  mainstream discourse for so long the  question of free speech as well  when  monarch that  podcast host that you just referenced  said  i think the government shouldn't have  the power to ban certain political  parties to me that is completely  uncontroversial that's the state of the  law in the united states because of our  constitution and when i defended him one  of the very few people who did  i was treated like a leper you know  people saying this freedom of speech is  a fascist ideology and we don't want it  here  which is so ironic given that the  hallmark of actual fascists is  censorship not free inquiry and free  discord  and it's even more ironic given that a  lot of people on the left who don't  believe in free speech here seem to  trust either the government currently  run by president bolsonaro or american  billionaires who control big tech who  they seem to be comfortable controlling  their political discourse what's  interest and i should say just because i  don't think our audience knows you did  more than complain about the censorship  of this podcast you helped him  get a new job so bless you for that  um  but the question of american media is  important here because bolsonaro no  matter what you think of him relies  pretty much exclusively on  american-owned tech platforms twitter  specifically to get his message out  doesn't that make him  totally vulnerable to censorship by  american companies well he has been  repeatedly censored by big tech  platforms he when speaking about kobit  was often censored when speaking about  the upcoming election is often censored  so facebook and google are essentially  dictating to brazilians what they can  and can't hear including from their own  democratically elected president and  again no matter what you think of  bolsonaro you should have to think that  that's a pretty  serious problem and i think it's a very  similar dynamic to what has happened in  the u.s where  the entire establishment essentially  united against trump and so all these  institutions that liberals on the left  in the united states have long held with  such contempt neocons and the security  state and corporate media all united  against trump and suddenly they were  viewed with such favor by the american  left and by am